<title>USA: USDA offers Estonia $6 mln under GSM-102 for FY97.</title>
<headline>USDA offers Estonia $6 mln under GSM-102 for FY97.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-10-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>The U.S. Agriculture Department Tuesday authorized $6 million in credit guarantees for sales of U.S. commodities to Estonia under the Export Credit Guarantee Program (GSM-102) for fiscal year 1997.</p>
<p>USDA said the farm goods covered include breeder livestock, protein meals, feed grains, rice, planting seeds, wheat flour and cotton.</p>
<p>Sales must be registered by Sept. 30, 1997, with exports no later than Nov. 30, 1997.</p>
